WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.467
-Guys, today's Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.534
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.434
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.868
and of course I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.601
So I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind just --

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.033
thank you -- I'd like to write
us some --

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.000
James, give us some thank-you
note writing music, please.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.834
♪♪

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.868
-He has, like,
a goatee just to mock you.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.234
-Yeah, that's kind
of weird to me.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.834
-He didn't even grow
a whole beard.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:25.367
-[ Laughs ]
-Wow.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.801
-He doesn't have a beard,
really.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.434
It's more of a, uh --
-It's like a goatee

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.634
or a Van Dyke.
-It's like a --

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:32.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.300
It's like a Mitch Miller-type
of vibe.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.701
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.200
[ Laughs ]

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.434
Or a Van Dyke mustache.
-I mean, I can shave this thing.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.968
I did it, I -- Tariq dared me,
I proved it,

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:46.501
I, you know, La Schmoove.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.167
-I don't got nothing to prove.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:55.234
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.567
-Don't edit that.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.901
[ Laughter ]
-Don't edit.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.434
-Man, La Schmoove, man.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.300
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.801
Thank you, Santa Con,

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.167
for looking like
a "Where's Waldo?"

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.501
for sober people.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.567
It's like, "Oh, that person.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.100
That person."

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.434
[ Applause ]

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:24.567
Thank you, car reindeer set,
for letting everyone on the road

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.634
know that you're a lot.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.501
-Let 'em go.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.868
-Just let 'em go.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.334
Let 'em pass you,
let 'em the other way,

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.133
we don't care, just -- yeah,
they've got something going on.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.167
-They got some issues.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:39.434
[ Imitating car horn,
scatting "La Cucaracha" ]

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.634
-Thank you, Harry and Meghan's
new Netflix documentary,

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.868
for getting King Charles to sign
up for Peacock.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:47.934
Ooh, well, there you go.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.100
That's one way to do it.
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.300
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.334
-[ Laughs ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.834
-Thank you, Spotify Wrapped,
for reminding me

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:01.601
of that one night in May I fell
asleep with whale sounds

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.501
on repeat.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.334
Whale sounds? That's my song?

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.601
-What?

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.634
-You listened to it
for 1,500 minutes.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:11.934
-1,500 minutes of whale sounds.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.868
Fart noises are number two.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.267
-Thank you, opening one window
while driving,

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.968
for making me feel like
I'm getting an MRI

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.267
in the middle of a tornado.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.234
It's like...
-[ Warbling sounds ]

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.267
[ Laughs ]

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:31.467
-Wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-
wub-wub-wub...

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:34.200
[ Singing "Chariots of Fire" ]
-Make it better, faster,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.934
stronger.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.400
-How's everything else going?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.400
How's that beard coming?

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.100
-It's throwing
the whole game off.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.901
-Yeah, beard's messing
with your brain.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.000
-It's just making me look, yeah.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.267
-I mean, you never had it,
you know, really properly

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.467
sort of, you know.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.934
-Wow.
-[Crowd] Oh!

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.567
-Wow. Properly sort of?

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:56.601
-I mean, you know...
-Properly sorted -- that --

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.234
-You never had it, like,
you know.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.434
Like --
-Like what you have?

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.467
-I mean, you could never
have what I have.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:02.567
-I don't --
-But, I mean --

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.634
-I don't live in the woods
for eight years.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.567
[ Laughter ]
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.701
You never had it, like,
you know, connecting and --

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.334
-It looks like you're wearing
a disguise.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:15.033
[ Laughter ]
-It's a Brawny paper towel.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.167
-Yeah, I mean, you can see
who it is.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.200
-What did Steve say yesterday?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.400
Your beard looks like
a COVID mask

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.267
with a hole cut out in it.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.434
-He's right!

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:27.467
He's got a point.

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.033
It's too thick.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.367
-Yeah, no.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:34.934
-[ Laughs ]
-Thank you,

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:36.534
office Christmas parties
for having the rule --

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.234
liquor before beer,
you're in the clear.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.634
Beer before liquor,
you'll see HR quicker.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.067
There you go, okay.

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.067
There you go.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:45.501
-I said that?

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.767
I said that?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.868
-Thank you, Aaron Judge,

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.334
or as your family now calls you,
Santa.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.367
There you have it, everybody.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.467
Those were our thank-you notes.

